WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.390
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.370
So cold…

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.210
It doesn’t snow here very often.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.340
Good morning!

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.970
Oh, good morning.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:36.560
The heavy snowfall is causing
some malfunctions in our systems.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:42.230
I decided to close the institute for a few days
so we could do maintenance.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.620
System maintenance?

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.520
What? The institute’s closed?!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.820
Where are we gonna get food?!

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.480
<i>That’s</i> what you’re worried about?

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:57.490
I’m sorry about this. It would be easier for us
if you went home in the meantime.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.580
Oh, Go!

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.580
You’re coming home tomorrow?

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.030
Sure! We’ll be waiting for you!

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.210
Take care!

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.930
Yeah! See you!

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.520
You have to tell your mom
that you're coming home?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.790
Yeah. She and Dad are both
really busy with work,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.100
so I’d rather not bother them
by coming home out of nowhere.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.850
Really…
What do they work with?

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.970
Dad’s a system engineer,
and Mom’s a programmer.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.860
They run a company together.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.590
Whenever systems break,
like what’s going on with the institute right now,

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.620
people like Mom and Dad get called in
to deal with it. It’s real tough.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:43.120
I don’t really get it,
but it <i>does</i> sound tough…

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.640
Hibunny.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.370
My family lives in an apartment,
so behave.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.510
I know.
I should get them something!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.720
The next day

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.470
I’m going home by bus.
How about you?

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.900
I’m taking the train.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.810
The train, huh?

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.390
How long does it take
to get to Masara Town?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.190
Okay, Hibunny, I got it!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.140
Go! You dropped something!

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.030
Hold on!

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.110
You forgot this!
Hey, you forgot this!

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.520
He’s gone…

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.010
Here we are, Hibunny!

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.010
It’s the seventh floor
in that building!

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.370
Now, let’s go visit my family!

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:52.690
PocketMonsters

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.110
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.690
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.410
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.280
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.620
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.290
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:12.790
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:18.050
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.640
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.560
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.310
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:39.320
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:43.530
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.870
Let's have a fight!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.580
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.410
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.750
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.420
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.760
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.260
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:12.390
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.190
I choose you!

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:23.200
Where is Karakara's Bone?
On a Snowy Day,

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.180
I’m home!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.600
Welcome home, Go!

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.390
Hibunny, this is my grandmother.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.570
Grandma, this is my partner;
Hibunny!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.630
Shibunny?
Those ears are wicked!

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.570
I’m glad you’re here.
Come on in!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.020
Star-shaped carrots!

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.900
I made them
thinking you’d be happy.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.650
Oh, of course!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.530
A souvenir for you, Grandma!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.720
Meat buns!

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.030
Oh, that’s lovely!

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.280
Thank you.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.910
I’m going to a local karaoke tournament today,
so I’ll share these with everybody there!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.230
I see. Have fun!

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.890
Hibunny and I will be
taking care of the house!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.550
I see you’ve got yourself
a good partner!

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:25.150
You should save the stew
for when Ikuo and Kurune come home.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.650
I’m sure they’ll try to finish up work quickly
so they can come see you!

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.060
Yeah, of course!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:36.900
All right, I’m off to go get
the karaoke tournament victory trophy!

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:43.690
Well? Think you can get it done?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.650
Yes. You?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.610
About five percent left, I guess.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.040
Then let’s hurry so
we can go home!

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.880
But for him to come home
so suddenly…

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.250
Did he cause some sort of trouble
and get kicked out?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.840
He couldn’t have!

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:05.260
Well, I guess he <i>was</i> always
cooped up inside his room…

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:07.920
Go.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:13.410
We’re sorry we have to work
through the holiday.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.420
We’ll try to wrap it up quickly,
so be good and wait for us.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.370
I’m totally fine! I’ve got tons of stuff
I wanna research.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:28.660
We’ve been so caught up in work
that we haven’t been able to spend time with him.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:33.090
Koharu is about the only
friend his age he’s got…

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:37.660
What if he didn't get along with
the people at the institute?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.940
Me, too…

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.670
This is Go Go Systems,
can I help you?

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.050
What… Now?

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.060
Yes… Very well. Of course.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:57.810
Hibunny, this is my room!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.990
Mom and Dad set this up for me!

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:09.240
I can get info on Mew
from all over the world!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.530
Amazing, yeah?

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.840
Go, go! Go, go!

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.320
It’s Mom.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.660
Hello?

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.640
Go? Where are you right now?

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.230
I’m at home.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.050
Welcome home.
We wish we could come home, too…

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.620
But another job
came in all of a sudden.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.690
There’s been a system malfunction
at the hospital by the station.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.610
So we might be late…

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.340
Got it. Don’t worry about me!

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:39.510
Grandma made stew!

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.510
What? I want some!

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:44.640
I’ll have some when I get back!
I’m starving!

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.750
We’ll try to
wrap this up quickly.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:48.830
Sorry.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.090
It’s totally fine! Later!

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.180
“Try to wrap this up quickly”, huh?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.670
We’re sorry we have to work
through the holiday.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:10.110
We’ll try to wrap it up quickly,
so be good and wait for us.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:16.230
I’m totally fine!
They don’t need to worry about me.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:22.230
Hibunny! Mom and Dad
are super cool!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:26.760
They fix systems up in no time at all
to help grant people’s wishes!

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.330
They’re like wizards, yeah?

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:33.390
I know!

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.450
Let’s go give this to Mom and Dad!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.460
They’re at the hospital by the station!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.150
And while we’re there,
we should give them…

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:48.010
Huh?

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.340
It’s gone!

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.230
Where’d I forget it?

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:57.350
Oh, well…
The stew’s better than nothing.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.050
It’s cold today, too…

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.060
Hibunny,
we’ll head through the park.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:13.700
What?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.480
Mankey? Karakara?

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:27.500
Karakara! Lonely Pokémon!
Ground type!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.270
It wears the skull of its dead mother
on its head!

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:37.010
It is said to cry loudly,
pining for the mother it will never see again!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.510
It always carries a Thick Bone!

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.380
Mankey! Pig Monkey Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:49.650
An extremely ill-tempered Pokémon
whose anger resonates even in its dreams!

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:56.660
Karakara clearly doesn’t
stand a chance here…

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.490
Hibunny?!

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:16.590
Hey, wait, Hibunny!

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.340
That bone must have been important.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.040
All right.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.490
I’ll get it back for you.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:57.340
Don’t cry! It’ll be fine!
Let’s find those Mankey.

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.890
We should ask everyone for help.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:08.030
Butterfree, Spear,
Strike, Subame!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.120
Sorry for bringing you
out in the cold…

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.870
But I’d like you to help us
get Karakara’s bone back.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:28.040
Get it? It looks like this.
Everybody look for this!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.270
All right! Find Mankey!
Off we…

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:39.810
…go!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.370
PocketMonsters

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.200
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:48.520
PocketMonsters

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:53.440
Ground
Karakara
PocketMonsters

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.340
Where did those Mankey go?

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:38.730
They can’t have gotten <i>that</i> far…

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.380
Let’s see… The apartment building
should be somewhere close…

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.530
That must be it!

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.200
Nobody home?

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:02.190
I’ll try calling.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.970
Call from Satoshi!
Call from Satoshi!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.140
Hello?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.350
That you, Go?

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.750
I’m at your apartment
right now.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.380
Director Sakuragi
told me the address.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.610
Where are you right now?

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:20.530
Well, I’m at the park…
Some stuff happened.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.860
Hey!

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.120
Go!

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.930
Satoshi! Thanks for the help.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.840
You can thank me later!

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:34.120
Did you find those Mankey?

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.340
Not yet.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:39.210
They can be pretty crafty…

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.770
I see… You’re luring them out
with a Nana Berry.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.770
That’s right!

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.250
There!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.410
Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.300
Hibunny! Lightning Speed!

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.460
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.190
Butterfree! Stun Spore!

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.330
Mankey!
Give back Karakara’s bone!

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.960
Where’d you leave it?

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:07.970
You lost it?!

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.060
Where?!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.520
What’s that mean?!

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.450
C’mon, cheer up, Karakara.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.310
It’ll be fine!
I promise we’ll find it!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:41.420
You look real carefully, too!

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:46.820
It might be buried in the snow.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.410
We’ve gotta find it
before it gets dark.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.810
Looks like it found something.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.550
Well, then, <i>you’re</i> up!

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:06.190
Good thing we finished quickly.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.190
Go is waiting. Let’s hurry home!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.310
Go?!

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.690
I don't really get it...

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.370
But that pond seems fishy!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:52.610
But if it’s in the pond…

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.060
That looks <i>really</i> cold…

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.860
I know just who to use!

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:15.950
Dewgong, huh? Yeah, Ice-type Pokémon
are resistant to the cold!

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:17.930
Counting on you, Dewgong!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.040
There!

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.780
Good for you!

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.720
Thanks, Satoshi.
And all of you, too!

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:04.510
Go!

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:08.350
Mom?! Dad?!

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.270
That was quite the shock…

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:14.860
We saw you flying on a Pokémon
on our way home!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:19.240
We were looking for
Karakara’s lost bone.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.530
You must be Satoshi.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.130
From Masara Town!

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.040
Well…

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:28.170
I hear Go’s been
relying on you quite a bit.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.340
Oh, no, not at all! Right, Go?

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.190
And you must be Hibunny?

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:39.500
You’re Satoshi’s Pikachu,
aren’t you?

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:41.680
What a cutie!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:45.620
And all these guys are my partners!

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.570
Karakara says it’s your partner, too!

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:59.320
Karakara…
Are you sure I can catch you?

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:21.220
I got Karakara!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:25.010
Karakara’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:29.350
You must be glad, Go.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:30.780
Yeah!

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.260
I hope we’ll get along.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.550
Now, let’s go home and eat!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:51.750
Actually, I was on the way
to bring you some stew.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.130
You were?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:58.910
I had another thing I wanted
to give you, too, but…

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.260
You mean this?

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:06.390
You dropped it
before you got on the bus.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.820
You mean you were here
to give me this?

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:11.900
You shouldn’t have…

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.520
I was!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.650
Thank you!

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:23.160
Don’t sweat it! Now hand it over
to your parents, already!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.100
Here…

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.290
What could it be?

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:31.210
Gloves?

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.540
Because it’s so cold…

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.670
Thank you!

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.070
You, too, Satoshi!

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.000
Don’t mention it!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.430
Satoshi, you should have
some stew with us!

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.150
For real?!

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.900
All right! I was starving!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:00.820
I got the victory trophy at
the karaoke tournament!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.230
Awesome!

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.280
You did it!

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:07.120
Let me see!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.270
Here!

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.330
I’m relieved.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:18.140
We must have made Go feel lonely,
being away with work so much…

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:21.620
But he’s made so many friends!

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:22.400
Yeah.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.010
As the meetings and
adventures keep coming,

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:31.080
Satoshi and Go continue
to grow with their Pokémon.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:35.560
With more amazing friends yet to meet,
on they... go!

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:45.940
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.310
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:48.450
(Pikachu → Mew Ver.)
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.020
Pokémon Shiritori
(Pikachu → Mew Ver.)

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:50.030
(Pikachu → Mew Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.280
Pokémon Shiritori (Pikachu → Mew Ver.)

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.570
Pikachu!

